    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "In the spring of 2026, individuals caught in the system's net surged to 8,268 along the southwest border as milder weather drew migrants toward the geopolitical boundary. The increase in apprehensions reflected a seasonal push against the state's enforcement perimeter, yet current policies correlate with low crossing figures overall. Meanwhile, the system's gatekeepers remained paralyzed, unable to resolve a funding dispute for the enforcement machine.",
