    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The regime's harsh policies have suppressed movement to historic lows along the U.S. border, but enforcement statistics showed a monthly increase in March. Crossing numbers remain near historical lows under asylum shutdown and deportation measures, even as milder spring weather conditions prompted a rise in border crossers apprehended. Political gridlock deepens over expanding state enforcement funding, leaving the legislative stalemate unresolved.",
